# House rule: one ignore = one justification + one removal condition. Every entry below concerns a
# transitive Go dependency embedded in the FrankenPHP/Caddy binary (/usr/local/bin/frankenphp), not
# our PHP code nor composer.lock. They will disappear once a FrankenPHP release rebuilds them with
# the fixed versions: rescan on every base image bump and drop the lines that became useless.
#
# FrankenPHP 1.12.6 (2026-07-20) is the latest release as of 2026-07-28 and predates both advisories,
# so there is nothing to bump to yet.

# kin-openapi v0.140.0, pulled in by smallstep/step-ca (Caddy's internal CA): fail-open authentication
# bypass in openapi3filter.ValidationHandler.Load(). The openapi3filter package is not linked into our
# binary — only openapi3 and routers are, and NoopAuthenticationFunc is absent
# (verified with `grep -ac 'NoopAuthenticationFunc' /usr/local/bin/frankenphp` => 0). Trivy reports the
# module from the Go build info, but the vulnerable code is not in the image.
# REMOVE once a FrankenPHP release ships kin-openapi >= 0.144.0.
GHSA-r277-6w6q-xmqw

# gRPC-Go v1.81.1: xDS RBAC and HTTP/2 rapid-reset vulnerabilities of the gRPC *server*. openchurch
# exposes no gRPC service — traffic is served by Caddy's HTTP server — and the xDS transport is not
# linked (`grep -ac 'google.golang.org/grpc/xds' /usr/local/bin/frankenphp` => 0).
# REMOVE once a FrankenPHP release ships grpc >= 1.82.1.
GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf

